# Generated by python -m ridge.deck_narrative --write. Scenario wording is
# rendered from assets/scenario-narrative-v1.json; do not retype it here.
pageType: content
audience: participant
background:
  type: solid
  color: "$paper"
elements:
  - elementId: tag
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 40, 400, 16]
    content: {style: "$tag", wrap: false, text: PART 1 · THE INCIDENT}
  - elementId: title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 66, 832, 34]
    content: {style: "$title", fontSize: 30, wrap: false, text: "How far the response got, and what is at stake"}
  - elementId: rule
    elementType: line
    bounds: [64, 116, 832, 2]
    viewBox: [832, 2]
    points: "0,1.0 832,1.0"
    curve: sharp
    border: {style: solid, width: 2, color: "$line"}
  - elementId: escalation-head
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 144, 396, 19]
    content: {fontSize: 15, bold: true, color: "$slate", wrap: false, text: HOW THE RESPONSE WENT}
  - elementId: escalation-rule
    elementType: line
    bounds: [64, 171, 396, 2]
    viewBox: [396, 2]
    points: "0,1.0 396,1.0"
    curve: sharp
    border: {style: solid, width: 2, color: "$slate"}
  - elementId: escalation
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 183, 396, 136]
    contractRef: exercise.escalation
    content:
      style: "$body"
      fontSize: 14
      text: |
        <p>The response moved in three steps and it moved badly. First a credential was reset, which is the correct instinct and does not end a session. Then a network review started, which is the correct second step. Neither step asked what the session could still reach, so the investigation is still open when your team takes it.</p>
  - elementId: stakes-head
    elementType: text
    bounds: [500, 144, 396, 19]
    content: {fontSize: 15, bold: true, color: "$slate", wrap: false, text: WHY IT MATTERS}
  - elementId: stakes-rule
    elementType: line
    bounds: [500, 171, 396, 2]
    viewBox: [396, 2]
    points: "0,1.0 396,1.0"
    curve: sharp
    border: {style: solid, width: 2, color: "$slate"}
  - elementId: stakes
    elementType: text
    bounds: [500, 183, 396, 159]
    contractRef: exercise.stakes
    content:
      style: "$body"
      fontSize: 14
      text: |
        <p>A superseded brief is still a real disclosure. Even after the service issued a replacement, the earlier version had already left the building, and nothing in the evidence can tell you who held it afterwards. If you stop at the first convincing answer you will hand the next shift a conclusion they cannot defend. If you overstate it, you will accuse an organisation of something the records do not show.</p>
  - elementId: attribution-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 374, 832, 16]
    content: {fontSize: 13, bold: true, color: "$amber", wrap: false, text: AND WHAT NO FINDING MAY SUPPORT}
  - elementId: attribution-rule
    elementType: line
    bounds: [64, 396, 832, 2]
    viewBox: [832, 2]
    points: "0,1.0 832,1.0"
    curve: sharp
    border: {style: solid, width: 2, color: "$amber"}
  - elementId: attribution
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 408, 832, 44]
    contractRef: boundaries.attribution
    content:
      style: "$body"
      fontSize: 14
      text: |
        <p>The evidence supports an unauthorised tool and an outbound transfer. It does not support naming a person, a group or a sponsor. Do not supply one in a finding.</p>
  - elementId: footer
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 505, 700, 15]
    content: {fontSize: 12, color: "#7E877F", wrap: false, text: OPERATION SILENT RIDGE — EXERCISE ONLY}
  - elementId: pagenum
    elementType: text
    bounds: [880, 505, 40, 15]
    content: {fontSize: 12, color: "#7E877F", align: [right, top], wrap: false, text: "3"}
